{title: 328 - Must Jesus Bear the Cross Alone}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #328 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 328}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Must Jesus bear the [C]cross alone, and [G]all the world go [D]free?
[G]No, there's a cross for [C]everyone, and [G]there's a cross [D7]for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]The [C]consecrated [G]cross [D]I'll bear
[G]till [C]He [G]shall [D7]set [G]me free;
[G]and then [C]go home [G]my crown [D]to wear,
[G]for [C]there's [G]a [D7]crown [G]for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Upon [C]the [G]crystal [D]pavement, down
[G][C]at [G]Jesus' [D7]pierced [G]feet,
[G]with [C]joy I'll [G]cast my [D]golden crown,
[G]and [C]His [G]dear [D7]name [G]repeat.
{end_of_verse}
